    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d109">

                <pb facs="0210" n="104" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg104"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 U.S.S.R./67: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-06-08T17:00:00-04:00">June 8, 1934—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>112. Your 124 and 125, June 8. In reply to constant inquiries from American
                    business men as to prospect of debt agreement we have replied that negotiations
                    are being carried on at Moscow with hope of a successful conclusion. We have not
                    interpreted temporary cessation as meaning abandonment. We have no thought of
                    taking up matter with Troyanovsky until we hear from you in answer to our
                    108.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
